  "body": "Refs #1448. Part of #1448.\n\nDepends on #3324 (the shared mechanism). Do not start before #3324 is merged. The `blocked` label goes when #3324 is closed.\n\n## What happens\n\n2D Adaptive puts its entry (helix, ramp or plunge) where its planner selects. The user cannot set where the tool enters the material or where the last pass ends. `sane.rs:71-87` refuses a start or an exit point on Adaptive2D. Adaptive2D has `links` and `entry` (`params.rs:226-273`).\n\n## Expected\n\n- Start: the planner enters the region at the pick. The engagement law then grows the cleared area from that place.\n- Exit: the last pass ends at the place in the region nearest the exit pick, or the exit is refused by name.\n- The trochoidal method and the arc turns keep their laws (`sane.rs:23`).\n\nSeam: `crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/mod.rs:142` (`AdaptiveSpec`), `:163` (`AdaptivePlan`), `:178` (`Planner`); `adaptive_troch.rs`.\n\n## Why effort:max\n\nThe adaptive planner chooses its seed and its growth order. A user seed is a change to that algorithm and to its engagement proof.\n\n## Laws a pick must keep (refused by name, never moved)\n\n- The helix or the ramp fits in the region at the pick. A tool that is not centre-cutting gets `CENTER_CUT_REFUSAL`.\n- The engagement limit holds from the first pass on.\n- The pick is inside the machinable region and outside each keep-out region.\n- The first traverse (`operation/first_traverse.rs:45`).\n\n## Done means\n\n- A pin test shows the entry at the pick, with golden CL, and no move over the engagement limit.\n- A pin test shows an exit at the pick, and one shows an impossible pick refused by name.\n- Undo and redo restore the previous path. MCP `edit_operation` sets the picks.\n- Every shipped Adaptive golden without a pick is byte-identical.\n\nSafety floor: this changes toolpaths and posted G-code.\n",
